      "nets": ["+24V", "G_RPP", "ATO_VALVE", "D_ATO"],
      "observed": "T3 (AON6407) is drawn in the +24V reverse-polarity protection path, while ATO_VALVE drives T5 (AO3400A), the low-side ATO switch. The specification identifies T3 (AON6407) as the ATO low-side switch.",
      "expected": "The specified AON6407 T3 should be the ATO_VALVE low-side switch, rather than being used in the reverse-polarity path with an AO3400A T5 switching the valve.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "POWER TRAIN: T3 AON6407; MAIN PUMP & VALVE DRIVERS: ATO_VALVE → T4 → T5 AO3400A → D_ATO (sheet 1, page 1)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch; Netlist: drives ATO_VALVE net (sheet 1, page 1)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The ATO valve is switched by a different MOSFET than specified, and the specified AON6407 is instead assigned to input protection. The substituted AO3400A may have lower current and thermal capability, so the valve may be unreliable or the switch may be overstressed if its load exceeds that device's limits.",
      "confidence": 0.83
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic assigns the AON6407 T3 to reverse-polarity protection and uses an AO3400A T5 for the ATO valve, contrary to the specification's stated ATO switch assignment. This component-role discrepancy could affect valve-switching capability."
}

